        <div class="wrap"><div class="col">
            <div class="eyebrow">Technology stack · Hardware</div>
            <h2>The physical side.</h2>
            <div class="cards">
                <div class="glass card"><div class="icon"><img src="/images/responsive_web_development.png" alt=""></div>
                    <div><h3>Arduino</h3><span class="sub">Microcontroller, firmware</span></div>
                    <p>Using microcontrollers and firmware to bridge software and hardware.</p></div>
                <div class="glass card"><div class="icon"><img src="/images/cms.png" alt=""></div>
                    <div><h3>Electronics</h3><span class="sub">Schematic, PCB design</span></div>
                    <p>Schematic and PCB design: electronics as the nervous system of a hardware product.</p></div>
                <div class="glass card"><div class="icon"><img src="/images/Octocat.png" alt=""></div>
                    <div><h3>Microprocessors</h3><span class="sub">Linux</span></div>
                    <p>Linux and microprocessor communication, from server configuration to microcontroller operations.</p></div>
                <div class="glass card"><div class="icon"><img src="/images/java-logo.png" alt=""></div>
                    <div><h3>IoT</h3><span class="sub">Internet of Things</span></div>
                    <p>Using the internet to control and connect devices into interconnected systems.</p></div>
            </div>
        </div></div>
    </section>

